2

1.12
“Street Lighting Service” refers to the provision of electricity for any street light,
pedestrian light, lamppost, street lamp, light standard, lamp standard, or any other raised source
of light on the edge of and within the right-of-way of a public road or walkway, which is turned
on or lit approximately at dusk at every night.

ARTICLE 2
GRANT OF FRANCHISE

2.1
Grant of Franchise.  The City of Cheyenne hereby grants to Cheyenne Light, Fuel
and Power Company, for the period specified in and subject to the conditions, terms and
provisions contained in this franchise, a non-exclusive right to furnish, sell and distribute
electricity to the City and its residents in the Franchise Area.  Subject to the conditions, terms
and provisions contained in this franchise, the City also hereby grants to the Company a non-
exclusive right to acquire, construct, install, locate, maintain, operate and extend into, within and
through the City all facilities reasonably necessary to furnish, sell and distribute electricity within
and through the city and a non-exclusive right to make reasonable use of the streets and other
public places, public rights-of-way, and dedicated easements as may be necessary to carry out
the terms of this franchise.  These rights shall extend to all areas of the city as it is now
constituted and to additional areas as the City may increase in size by annexation or otherwise.
Electric service territory is defined by Attachment A and Attachment B.  For the purposes of this
franchise, the word “furnish” shall refer to the use of facilities to supply and distribute electricity,
but shall not include the generation of electricity.

2.2
Street Lighting Service.  The rights granted in this franchise encompass the non-
exclusive franchise to provide street lighting service to the City and the provisions of this
franchise apply with full and equal force to the street lighting service provided by the Company.
Wherever reference is made to the sale of electricity or to the provision of electric service in this
franchise, these references shall be deemed to include the provision of street lighting service.
Wherever reference is made to Company facilities, equipment, system or plant in this franchise,
this reference shall be deemed to include Company-owned street lighting facilities, equipment,
system and plant.

2.3
Term of Franchise.  This franchise shall take effect on January 1, 2013.  The term
of this franchise shall be for twenty-five (25) years, expiring on December 31, 2037.

ARTICLE 3
FRANCHISE FEE

3.1
Franchise Fee.  In consideration for the grant of this franchise, the Company shall
pay the City a sum equal to a percentage of all gross revenues received from the sale of
electricity as follows:

a.
One percent (1.0%) of gross revenues derived from all customers within
the certified service area of the Company as approved by the PSC, excluding other
franchised areas.

b.
Two percent (2.0%) of gross revenues derived from all customers within
the City from January 1, 2013 through December 31, 2037, provided however, that the
City reserves unto itself the unilateral right to increase said franchise fee by no more than
one-half of one percent (.5%) by amendment to this franchise ordinance enacted during
the period of time from January 1, 2020 through March 1, 2020, during the period of time
from January 1, 2027 through March 1, 2027, and during the period of time from January
1, 2034 through March 1, 2034, and provided further that in no event shall said franchise
fee increase by more than one and one-half percent (1.5%) during the term of this
franchise.  It is the specific intent of this subsection that the City shall have the unilateral
right, in the exercise of its sole and absolute discretion, to increase said franchise fee,
```

### Page 7 of 16

```text
3
subject to the limitations contained herein, but shall not be obligated to do so.

c.
The City will cooperate with Company by providing Company with a map
of its corporate limits (the “Map”).  The Map shall be of sufficient detail to assist
Company in determining whether their customers reside within the City’s corporate
limits.  The Map shall serve as the basis for determining Company’s obligation hereunder
to collect and pay the franchise fee from customers; provided, however, that if the City’s
corporate limits are changed by annexation or otherwise, the City will provide the
updated Map to the Company.  Company’s obligation to collect and pay the franchise fee
from customers within an annexed area shall not commence until sixty (60) days after
such Company’s receipt of a revised Map or other information as is reasonably necessary
for Company to identify the customers in the annexed area obligated to pay the franchise
fee.  The City will cooperate to provide copies of annexation ordinances to Company on a
timely basis to ensure appropriate franchise fee collection from customers within the
corporate limits of the City as set forth in this section 3.

3.2
Payment Contingency.  Cheyenne Light, Fuel and Power Company shall not be
liable for the payments required under Paragraph 3.1.a through Paragraph 3.1.b above for
consumers not served by the Company or those served by other franchise holders.

3.3
Payment Schedule.  For the franchise fee owed on revenues received after the
effective date of this franchise, payment shall be made in monthly installments not more than
thirty (30) days following the close of the month for which payment is to be made.  Initial and
final payments shall be prorated for the portions of the months at the beginning and end of the
term of this ordinance.  All payments shall be made to the City Clerk.  The City Clerk, or other
authorized representatives, shall have access to the books of the Company for the purpose of
auditing or checking to ascertain that the franchise fee has been correctly computed and paid.

If it is determined that a mistake was made in the payment of any franchise fee required
hereunder, unless otherwise agreed between the City and Company, such mistake shall be
corrected promptly upon discovery such that any under-payment by Company shall be paid
within sixty (60) days of reasonable recalculation of the amount due, and any over-payment by
Company shall be deducted from the next payment or successive payments of such franchise fee
due by Company to the City; provided, that neither party shall have the obligation to correct a
mistake that is discovered more than three (3) years after the occurrence thereof.

3.4
Change of Franchise Fee and Other Franchise Terms.  The Company shall, upon
request, report to the City within sixty (60) days of the execution of a subsequent franchise
granted by another municipality to the Company within the State of Wyoming or of any event
that could have a significant financial impact on the consideration to be paid by the Company to
the City hereunder.  If the Governing Body decides the consideration shall be changed, it shall
provide for such change by Ordinance; provided, however, that the consideration is not higher
than the highest consideration paid by the Company to any municipality within the State of
Wyoming.  For purposes of this section, “consideration” means the franchise fee established in
Article 3, Section 1 and also includes any other provision which is of similar significant financial
benefit to the City.

3.5
Franchise Fee Payment in Lieu of Other Fees and Charges.  In connection with
the operation of facilities to furnish, sell and distribute electricity within the City, as described in
Section 2.1 of this franchise, the Company shall be exempt from the requirements of Titles 5 and
15 of the Cheyenne City Code pertaining, respectively, to Business Licensing and Buildings and
Construction.  Payment of the franchise fee by the Company is accepted by the City in lieu of
any occupancy tax, license tax, or similar tax or charge on the privilege of doing business in the
City, but does not exempt the Company from any lawful taxation upon its property or any other
tax not related to the operation of its facilities to furnish, sell and distribute electricity as
described in Section 2.1 of this franchise.  Any independent contractor engaged by the Company
to perform construction work as described in Section 5.44.020 of the Cheyenne City Code must
obtain a City Contractor’s License.
